{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>He guards his mouth</b> — from speaking evil, then he keeps his life from trouble." "<b>Opens wide</b> — opens, from ותפשקי רגליך. Meaning: he opens his lips to speak what is not proper — ruin comes upon him."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:27.845977294Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}